nts-missing-title = The clock is not kept by a client that can authenticate servers
nts-missing-summary = chrony is not installed. Without it the time comes from plain NTP or nothing, and anyone on the path can change it. Install chrony, then turn this on.
nts-off-title = The clock takes time from servers it cannot authenticate
nts-off-summary = chrony has no NTS source. A forged time answer can break certificate checks and logs.
nts-may-affect-firewall-4460 = NTS asks each server for keys on TCP port 4460 first. A firewall that blocks it keeps the clock on its other sources.
nts-may-affect-clock = Time comes from the chosen servers in addition to the ones already set; IbexWall does not remove the distro's own.
detect-time-title = What keeps your clock today
detect-time-chrony-nts = chrony is running with { $sources } authenticated (NTS) sources. A forged time answer would be refused.
detect-time-chrony-plain = chrony keeps the clock from { $sources } sources that cannot be authenticated. A suggested setup that adds an authenticated source is ready to review below.
detect-time-chrony-unreadable = chrony is installed but its settings could not be read, so nothing is suggested.
detect-time-timesyncd = The clock is kept by systemd-timesyncd, which cannot authenticate servers. Install chrony, then come back here: { $install }
detect-time-ntpd = The clock is kept by ntpd, which IbexWall does not manage. For authenticated time, install chrony: { $install }
detect-time-none = No time service was found. Install chrony, then come back here: { $install }
